{"title":"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circles of diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inch and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches have the same center. The smaller circle is painted red, and the portion outside the smaller circle and inside the larger circle is painted blue. What is the ratio of the blue-painted area to the red-painted area? \n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2006amc10b04.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/4a/2006amc10b04.gif\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d1406ece86163432de4a6d530399586657459af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2\\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 3\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 6\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 8\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area painted red is equal to the area of the smaller circle and the area painted blue is equal to the area of the larger circle minus the area of the smaller circle. \n</p><p>So we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d37c9f484cc23142d62c049c710cdd9492af7cef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} A_{red}&amp;=\\pi\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\ A_{blue}&amp;=\\pi\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2-\\pi\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2=2\\pi\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"250\" height=\"99\" />\n</p><p>So the desired ratio is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc284c5f19869d04e3dc6aa1db4377dc331da45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A_{blue}}{A_{red}}=\\frac{2\\pi}{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}=2\\cancel{\\pi}\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\cancel{\\pi}}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"251\" height=\"46\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B\">2006 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<b